---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="The current privacy boundary for the static Servotab website and public support surfaces."
>
  <PageIntro
    index="05 / Privacy"
    title="A static site with a small data surface."
    description="Servotab.com has no account system, backend, database, analytics, advertising, or first-party tracking. Hosting and external services retain their own boundaries."
  />

  <article class="legal-document shell">
    <div class="legal-grid">
      <aside class="legal-aside">Last updated<br />30 August 2026</aside>
      <div class="legal-prose">
        <section>
          <h2>The website</h2>
          <p>
            This site is delivered as static files. It does not provide sign-in,
            user accounts, a product database, a first-party feedback form,
            analytics, advertising, tracking pixels, or first-party tracking cookies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Hosting and ordinary request data</h2>
          <p>
            The site is intended to be served through Cloudflare. Like an ordinary
            hosting and security layer, Cloudflare may process request information
            such as network address, user agent, requested URL, and timestamps to
            deliver and protect the site or maintain service logs. Cloudflare’s
            settings, policies, and retention practices govern that provider-side
            processing; this page does not promise a specific provider retention period.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>The Servotab product</h2>
          <p>
            Servotab’s planned public form is a skills-only engineering method layer.
            It does not add a Servotab account or product dashboard. Codex, repositories,
            browsers, terminals, tools, and external services used during engineering
            work remain governed by their own settings, permissions, and privacy terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Public support</h2>
          <p>
            Support links lead to a public GitHub issue tracker. Information submitted
            there is shared with GitHub and may be visible to anyone. Remove secrets,
            private code, personal data, account details, local paths, and private
            transcripts before posting. See the <a href="/support">support guide</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>External links</h2>
          <p>
            Links to GitHub, OpenAI, Cloudflare, or other sites leave servotab.com.
            Those services apply their own terms and privacy practices.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
